Q1. Why do we need Docker Networking?

Interview Ready Answer

Docker Networking enables communication between Docker containers,
between the host machine and containers, and between containers and
external networks. It allows multi-container applications such as
Spring Boot and MySQL to communicate securely and efficiently.

Definition

Docker Networking
- Communication mechanism for Docker containers.
- Connects containers with each other and external systems.

Purpose

• Container-to-container communication.
• Host-to-container communication.
• Container-to-external network communication.
• Enable multi-container applications.

======================================================================

Q2. What are the default Docker Networks?

Interview Ready Answer

Docker provides three default network types:

Bridge
- Default network for standalone containers.
- Allows containers on the same bridge network to communicate.

Host
- Shares the host machine's network stack.
- No separate network namespace is created.

None
- Disables networking for the container.
- Container has no network connectivity.

Purpose

• Bridge → General container communication.
• Host → High-performance networking.
• None → Isolated containers.

======================================================================

Q3. Which command lists all Docker Networks?

Interview Ready Answer

The following command lists all Docker networks available on the local
Docker host.

docker network ls

Purpose

• View available Docker networks.
• Verify existing networks.
• Manage networking.

======================================================================

Q4. Which command creates a new Docker Network?

Interview Ready Answer

A custom Docker network is created using:

docker network create <network_name>

Containers connected to the same custom network can communicate with
each other in an isolated environment.

Purpose

• Create isolated container networks.
• Enable communication between related containers.
• Improve application organization.

======================================================================

Q5. Which command inspects a Docker Network?

Interview Ready Answer

The following command displays detailed information about a Docker
network.

docker network inspect <network_name>

It shows:

• Network ID
• Driver
• Connected Containers
• Subnet
• Gateway
• Network Configuration

Purpose

• Troubleshoot networking.
• Verify connected containers.
• Inspect network configuration.

